WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.877
This query searches for duplicate groups using normalized email and normalized name.

00:00:05.877 --> 00:00:09.547
The email is trimmed and converted to lowercase.

00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:15.912
The name has extra spaces removed and is given consistent display capitalization.

00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:20.457
Then the query groups records by those normalized values.

00:00:20.457 --> 00:00:23.682
Only groups with more than one row are returned.

00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:31.333
The query also collects the source identifiers so you can see which records belong to the candidate group.

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:40.613
Imagine that one record contains Jane Smith with extra spaces and another contains the same name with different

00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:45.918
capitalization. Without normalization, SQL may treat them as different values.

00:00:45.918 --> 00:00:47.868
After normalization, they may fall into the same group.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:53.403
That does not prove they are the same person.

00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:57.229
It gives us stronger evidence that the records deserve review.
